 the tee log file! rtk saves full output to a log: ~/.local/share/rtk/tee/*.log—but I can't read files without a shell... however grep is possible. I can grep the log file! The log contains the full (pre-compression) output with match locations. But I still don't know which line.\n\nBetter approach: grep patterns that show which function is calling what. Grep the line with \"i915_driver_register\" and the surrounding lines—I can't get context. Alternative: grep \"^\\treturn i915_driver_register|^\\tret = i915_driver_register|^int i915_driver_probe|^static int i915_driver\"—rtk compresses output per call. Without -n, I can't tell the position. Hmm, without line numbers it's hard to figure out the enclosing function.\n\nThe first result of the \"int i915_\" grep shows the function definition order. In the upstream i915 (6.x), the call chain: i915_driver_probe → i915_driver_early_probe → i915_driver_mmio_probe → i915_driver_hw_probe → i915_driver_register. Let me verify by grepping for \"i915_driver_register(i915);\" and \"i915_driver_hw_probe\" within the file—grep only outputs matched lines. To identify the enclosing function, could I grep a distinctive string that appears near the call site? The call is \"ret = i915_driver_register(i915);\". Lines right before it in the upstream i915_driver_hw_probe: \"if (i915->params.enable_fsc) ...\" hmm.\n\nAlternative approach: use rtk against the tee log file. That contains the full grep output (pre-compression), probably line numbers? Let me grep the log file \"1787748697_grep_0_ivers_gpu_drm_i915_i915_driver_c.log\" for \"i915_driver_register\"—the log might contain line numbers. Try: path=~/.local/share/rtk/tee/1787748697_grep_0_ivers_gpu_drm_i915_i915_driver_c.log, pattern=\"i915_driver_register\".\n\nActually, even simpler: run rtk grep with the pattern \"i915_driver_register(i915\" to get the exact call site line. Then find the enclosing function: grep for the definition order of \"i915_driver_hw_probe\" and the call \"i915_driver_hw_probe(\". Upstream knowledge should be enough to confirm, but let me verify with grep for \"i915_driver_hw_probe\" in i915_driver.c."}}
